Subject: A layout hook retries while rows of its digest are unbuilt

What this does
  - `JSFunctionBytecode` gains `aot_layout_tries`. The first-construct layout hook (`js_aot_layout_fn_hook`) used to drop its mark after one attempt per bytecode. When the unit still has an unbuilt row for the bytecode's digest it now re-arms the mark as a countdown of 250 constructs (the constructs in between only decrement it, no digest is computed), at most 16 times; with nothing pending it drops the mark as before.

Why we need it
  Classes made by one function (Prototype.js's Class.create) share a bytecode digest. The unit builds each class's layout row against the closure its constant path names, and a class defined after the first construct is not there when the first attempt runs. A digest with one row, or all rows built, behaves exactly as before.

Soundness
  The hook only builds layouts the unit already owns; the retry never changes what a built layout means. Cost is a decrement per construct while rows are pending, bounded by 16 x 250 constructs.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -1981,0 +1982 @@
+    uint8_t aot_layout_tries;   /* attempts the layout hook has made for this bytecode while rows of its digest were still unbuilt (see js_aot_layout_fn_hook) */
@@ -66183,0 +66185 @@
+    b->aot_layout_tries = 0;
@@ -67017,0 +67020,5 @@
+    /* between attempts the flag counts constructs down (cheap: no digest) */
+    if (b->aot_layout_ctor > 1) {
+        b->aot_layout_ctor--;
+        return;
+    }
@@ -67024,4 +67031,11 @@
-    /* One attempt per bytecode: the layout is built (or refused) from the first
-       constructor object that constructs, so the mark is dropped whatever the
-       answer and every later construct skips the hash. */
-    b->aot_layout_ctor = 0;
+    /* One attempt per bytecode, unless rows of its digest are still unbuilt: the rows of classes
+       made by one function (every Class.create class) are built by each class's constant path, and
+       a class defined after the first construct is not there yet. Retry after 250 constructs, at
+       most 16 times; a digest with nothing pending drops the mark as before, so every later
+       construct skips the hash. */
+    if (&qjs_aot_layout_ctor != NULL && b->aot_layout_tries < 16 && qjs_aot_layout_ctor(dg)) {
+        b->aot_layout_tries++;
+        b->aot_layout_ctor = 250;
+    } else {
+        b->aot_layout_ctor = 0;
+    }
